# tools/w/witness_claim_check_witness.rish -- a witness reads its own claim natively (REDS %76 -> #85).
#
# The lantern that fired twice, now a loom. A witness checking its GREEN line with
#   run ["sh" "-c" "printf '%s' '${out}' | grep -q 'the source's window' && echo yes"]
# hands captured program output to the shell inside a single-quoted word, where one apostrophe closes
# the quote early -- the grep misses a truly-GREEN run and the witness reds while the code is sound.
# REDS %76 caught it at HUNK49 and taught the convention; REDS %85 caught the same shape again in the
# image family, because a template written before the rule kept seeding fragile checks forward. The
# convention now stands checkable: read the claim with Rishi's native `contains`, where an apostrophe
# is only a letter.
#
# Two rosters, by what this pier can prove: every runnable tools/*.rish is ENFORCED at zero captured-
# output interpolations inside shell quotes; the four device-gated host scripts (HAWM adb/Seva, SETU
# hearth carry, TUBE install proof) are REPORTED as a ratchet, since their conversion wants a phone or
# an outer terminal to witness. A planted fragile control proves the RED path on metal, so the guard
# can never quietly stop guarding. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/w/witness_claim_check_witness.rish

say "witness-claim-check: Language EN -- every witness that runs on this pier reads its own claim natively, so the shell can never lie about a module that is sound."
say "witness-claim-check: Style Radiant -- a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom; the convention REDS %76 taught is a check rather than a habit."
say "witness-claim-check: Lens TAME -- measurement beats memory; the guard counts the sites and a planted fragile control proves the RED path on metal."

let green = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/witness_claim_check_scan.sh"]
assert green.ok else "witness-claim-check: living scan must exit 0 -- ${green.out}"
assert green.out contains "enforce=honored" else "witness-claim-check: want the runnable witnesses enforced clean"
assert green.out contains "advisory=ratchet_report" else "witness-claim-check: want the device-gated remainder reported"
assert green.out contains "control_kept=honored" else "witness-claim-check: want the fragile control kept fragile"
assert green.out contains "verdict=ok" else "witness-claim-check: want verdict ok"

let red = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/witness_claim_check_scan.sh" "prove-red"]
assert (red.ok == false) else "witness-claim-check: prove-red must refuse"
assert red.out contains "RED_shell_grep_claim_check_caught" else "witness-claim-check: prove-red want the fragile control caught"

say "GREEN: witness-claim-check -- every runnable witness reads its claim natively, the device-gated remainder is ratcheted, the fragile control is caught (REDS %85 prevention on metal)."
